[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3724577765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114742#issuecomment-3724577765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114742","id":3724577765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eAIvl","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-08T16:08:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-08T16:08:20Z","body":"I expect this to break lots of existing tilemap spacebar heaters.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3724577765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3725242408","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114742#issuecomment-3725242408","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114742","id":3725242408,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eCrAo","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-08T19:02:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-08T19:03:27Z","body":"> tilemap spacebar heaters\r\n\r\nSorry, no idea what does this mean. 🙃\r\n\r\n> I expect this to break lots of existing tilemap\r\n\r\nNote that this change affects only tiles transformed within the TileMapLayer/TileMap cells (such transformation flags are stored per cell). This does not affect the original navigation polygon of the tile, including alternative tiles within the TileSet which have their own set of flip_h/flip_v/transpose flags, and their own navigation polygon (these are stored in the TileSet).\r\n\r\nSo I'd expect someone would already be dealing with broken navigation polygons in case they'd be using per-cell transformations (flips/transpose), as presented in the first 2 rows of the example images `before` in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114742#issue-3793287255.\r\nI can see that someone could try to work around these quirks, and thus would outline only the tiles not creating holes, but this still would be a workaround for the inconsistency `before`. Anyway, if a tile navigation is not outlined then it should correctly produce a not-hole both before/after.\r\nSo I don't expect this change to break user projects (besides probably some edge case I can't think of 🤔).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3725242408/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3726548588","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114742#issuecomment-3726548588","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114742","id":3726548588,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eHp5s","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T00:33:30Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T00:33:57Z","body":"> Sorry, no idea what does this mean. 🙃\r\n\r\nhttps://xkcd.com/1172/\r\n\r\nWhat I meant by that is, that this change will likely break some unknown amounts of existing projects that have build their entire level layout around this bug behavior. We will not know before but they will come screaming at us when this gets merged without an option that they can get back to the old behavior.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3726548588/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728530344","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114742#issuecomment-3728530344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114742","id":3728530344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ePNuo","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T11:30:48Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T11:30:48Z","body":"> https://xkcd.com/1172/\r\n\r\nOh, saw it many times, didn't connected the dots. 😄\r\n\r\n> What I meant by that is, that this change will likely break some unknown amounts of existing projects that have build their entire level layout around this bug behavior. We will not know before but they will come screaming at us when this gets merged without an option that they can get back to the old behavior.\r\n\r\nThat's possible, yes (and inevitable for lots of bugfixes). But to be clear, do you suggest we should somehow provide an option to get the previous inconsistent/buggy behavior? Or do you only warn to take this into consideration?\r\nI originally did consider how breaking the change is, and I still can't think of a valid use case which this change would break. Meaning I expect it to break projects only in some super rare/strange cases, pretty much everyone should not be affected by this. Given how broken the behavior \"before\" is for transformed cells (again: non-transformed cells are unaffected), I'd expect anyone trying to use it before to just ditch it / not use transformed cells because of that (when combined like that with some outer/enclosing polygon), instead of making some strange workarounds this PR would break.\r\nSo I do not consider this to as a breaking change (unless proven wrong by an example use case (now), or an issue report (after merge)).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728530344/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728624696","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114742#issuecomment-3728624696","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114742","id":3728624696,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ePkw4","user":{"login":"groud","id":6093119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwOTMxMTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6093119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud","html_url":"https://github.com/groud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/groud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T12:00:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T12:00:22Z","body":"It's fine. The only thing it would really change is the navigation behavior a bit, leading to more optimized paths. I don't think anyone would have their game rely on suboptimal paths.\r\n\r\n>  I originally did consider how breaking the change is, and I still can't think of a valid use case which this change would break. Meaning I expect it to break projects only in some super rare/strange cases, pretty much everyone should not be affected by this. Given how broken the behavior \"before\" is for transformed cells (again: non-transformed cells are unaffected), I'd expect anyone trying to use it before to just ditch it / not use transformed cells because of that (when combined like that with some outer/enclosing polygon), instead of making some strange workarounds this PR would break.\r\n\r\nAccording to the pictures, it was not even broken before. It would just work, with maybe less performances and suboptimal paths, but it would still work anyway if I understand correctly. \r\n\r\nIt's not a breaking change for me either.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3728624696/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3733646137","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114742#issuecomment-3733646137","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114742","id":3733646137,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eius5","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-10T22:53:21Z","updated_at":"2026-01-10T22:53:21Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3733646137/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]